{"seq":14,"slug":"concurrency-models","title":"并发模型","stage":"DONE","category":"languages","chapterCount":4,"docCount":14,"url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models","rating":{"composite":3.78,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 并发模型 简介\n\n现代的计算机几乎都拥有多个处理核心；现代的程序往往需要同时处理许多任务——响应众多用户的请求、同时下载多个文件、在计算的同时保持界面流畅。要充分利用多核硬件、要让程序同时做多件事，就必须让程序\"并发\"地执行。然而，并发编程是出了名的困难——它充满了微妙、难以重现的错误。为了驾驭并发的复杂，人们发展出了多种不同的\"并发模型\"——它们是组织并发程序的不同方式、不同范式。\n\n本知识库面向有一定编程基础、希望跨越具体语言理解并发本质的读者，分四章讲解并发的核心困难、共享内存与异步、消息传递、以及其他模型与选择。\n\n**第一章·并发基础**阐明并发的含义（与\"并行\"的区分）、并发为何困难（共享数据的竞态、执行顺序的不确定、同步的复杂）、以及不同并发模型的概貌。\n\n**第二章·共享内存与异步**深入两类基础模型——多线程共享内存（直观却带来竞态与锁的两难）、以及异步与事件循环（以单线程的非阻塞调度高效处理大量等待）。\n\n**第三章·消息传递**剖析从根本上规避共享之困难的范式——\"以通信取代共享\"，包括 Actor 模型与 CSP，及其安全、解耦、适合分布式的优势。\n\n**第四章·其他模型与意义**介绍软件事务内存、数据并行、协程、不可变性等其他机制，并上升到如何选择并发模型、以及贯穿全章的核心智慧。\n\n建议按章节顺序阅读。第一章建立整体认知与核心困难，第二章理解共享内存的困难与异步的出路，第三章掌握消息传递这一根本范式，第四章拓展其他机制并上升到选择与意义。阅读时不妨始终把握一条主线：并发因共享数据的竞态、执行顺序的不确定、同步的复杂而困难重重；人们发展出多种并发模型以不同方式驾驭它，而贯穿其中的核心智慧是——\"共享可变状态是并发之困难的根源，减少或消除它（通过不共享的消息传递、或不可变性）是驾驭并发最根本的途径\"。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"concurrency-foundations","title":"第一章 并发基础","docCount":3,"url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/concurrency-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-is-concurrency","title":"什么是并发","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/concurrency-foundations/what-is-concurrency"},{"seq":2,"slug":"why-concurrency-is-hard","title":"并发为何困难","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/concurrency-foundations/why-concurrency-is-hard"},{"seq":3,"slug":"overview-of-models","title":"并发模型的不同思路","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/concurrency-foundations/overview-of-models"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"shared-memory-and-async","title":"第二章 共享内存与异步","docCount":4,"url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/shared-memory-and-async","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"threads-and-shared-memory","title":"线程与共享内存","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/shared-memory-and-async/threads-and-shared-memory"},{"seq":2,"slug":"race-conditions","title":"竞态条件","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/shared-memory-and-async/race-conditions"},{"seq":3,"slug":"locks-and-synchronization","title":"锁与同步及其困难","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/shared-memory-and-async/locks-and-synchronization"},{"seq":4,"slug":"async-and-events","title":"异步与事件循环","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/shared-memory-and-async/async-and-events"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"message-passing","title":"第三章 消息传递","docCount":3,"url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/message-passing","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"message-passing-idea","title":"消息传递的核心思想","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/message-passing/message-passing-idea"},{"seq":2,"slug":"actor-model","title":"Actor 模型","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/message-passing/actor-model"},{"seq":3,"slug":"csp-model","title":"CSP 模型","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/message-passing/csp-model"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"other-models-and-significance","title":"第四章 其他模型与意义","docCount":4,"url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/other-models-and-significance","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"software-transactional-memory","title":"软件事务内存","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/other-models-and-significance/software-transactional-memory"},{"seq":2,"slug":"data-parallelism-and-coroutines","title":"数据并行与协程","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/other-models-and-significance/data-parallelism-and-coroutines"},{"seq":3,"slug":"immutability","title":"不可变性与函数式的角色","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/other-models-and-significance/immutability"},{"seq":4,"slug":"significance","title":"意义与选择","url":"/h/languages/concurrency-models/other-models-and-significance/significance"}]}]}